24/2/2026 ✅Data Streams
Notes:-
It is usually Linux Operating Concept 
Any Process have 3 stream, But they all are duplex stream at the end

stdin it is a readable Stream it connect keyboard to our process. The typing part
stdout it is a writable Stream connect process to monitor. The display part
stderr it is also writable Stream connect process to monitor. The error part

console uses process.stdout behind the scenes (NodeJS official Docs Says)

Help of this we can connect any two process and do data sharing and build connection

Example:-
using child_Process net module in NodeJS we can run process in other process and import the process stdout and bring to our main NodeJs application and play with it

Code Examples (./examples/ folder):-
  1_stdin_stdout_stderr.js    → stdin, stdout, stderr demo (interactive)
  2_piping_stdin_to_stdout.js → piping stdin → stdout (interactive)
  3_child_process_streams.js  → child_process: spawn, read stdout, write stdin, pipe 2 processes
  4_console_vs_stdout.js      → proves console.log uses process.stdout internally
  5_process_to_process.js     → full inter-process communication (send data ↔ receive results)

